---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url";
---
<Base title="Applications — SciencesLoop" description="Proposed applications for SciencesLoop evidence-gated scientific workflows, beginning with offline electrochemistry analysis in brownfield laboratories." alternatePath={u("/zh/applications/")}>
  <div class="sl-page">
    <section class="sl-page-hero"><span class="sl-chip proposed">Application direction · proposed</span><h1>Start beside the instrument, not inside it.</h1><p class="sl-lead">The initial product direction is a software layer for offline electrochemistry workflows: ingest existing CV/EIS exports, evaluate evidence quality, surface anomalies, preserve provenance, and route consequential decisions to a human.</p></section>

    <section class="sl-section"><div class="sl-section-head"><span>01 · First wedge</span><h2>Electrochemistry evidence review.</h2></div><div class="sl-grid three"><article class="sl-card"><span class="sl-index">Input</span><h3>Brownfield exports</h3><p>Work from existing instrument files and laboratory metadata without claiming direct control of the instrument.</p></article><article class="sl-card"><span class="sl-index">Analysis</span><h3>CV/EIS inference</h3><p>Apply bounded preprocessing, feature extraction, anomaly checks, and uncertainty-aware comparison.</p></article><article class="sl-card"><span class="sl-index">Output</span><h3>Evidence packet</h3><p>Return a trace linking source data, transformations, claims, uncertainty, and the human approval state.</p></article></div></section>

    <section class="sl-section sl-dark"><div class="sl-section-head"><span>02 · Boundary</span><h2>Not an autonomous instrument controller.</h2></div><div class="sl-boundary"><div><span class="sl-chip working">In development</span><ul><li>Offline file ingestion and schema checks</li><li>Deterministic preprocessing and replay</li><li>Evidence gaps, anomaly flags, and review states</li><li>Interfaces for human approval</li></ul></div><div><span class="sl-chip risk">Outside current claim</span><ul><li>Sending commands to laboratory instruments</li><li>Validated closed-loop wet-lab experiments</li><li>Inter-laboratory transfer performance</li><li>Production deployment or safety certification</li></ul></div></div></section>

    <section class="sl-section"><div class="sl-section-head"><span>03 · Validation path</span><h2>Partnership follows the evidence need.</h2></div><div class="sl-grid two"><article class="sl-card"><span class="sl-chip proposed">Near-term</span><h3>Public and permissioned data</h3><p>Define acceptance criteria and test bounded workflow behavior on attributable datasets and physics-based or deterministic cases.</p></article><article class="sl-card"><span class="sl-chip proposed">Future option</span><h3>Laboratory validation</h3><p>A university, customer laboratory, or DOE user facility could become a future validation collaborator when access and scope make sense. No National Laboratory or university partnership is currently claimed, and such a partnership is not presented as a prerequisite for the software concept.</p></article></div></section>

    <section class="sl-section"><div class="sl-section-head"><span>04 · Expansion logic</span><h2>Generalize the evidence contract, not the marketing claim.</h2></div><div class="sl-roadmap"><div><b>Now</b><strong>Electrochemistry</strong><span>Offline CV/EIS evidence review</span></div><i>→</i><div><b>Next</b><strong>Adjacent instruments</strong><span>Reuse provenance and approval patterns</span></div><i>→</i><div><b>Later</b><strong>Cross-workflow orchestration</strong><span>Only after validation supports transfer</span></div></div></section>

    <section class="sl-section sl-contact"><div><h2>Bring a real workflow boundary.</h2><p>SciencesLoop is interested in validation problems with attributable data, clear decisions, and measurable acceptance criteria.</p></div><a class="sl-button primary" href="mailto:luzhang@sciencesloop.com?subject=SciencesLoop%20validation%20conversation">Discuss a validation use case</a></section>
  </div>
</Base>
